            "review_title": "Review at Bia Hoi Ha Noi",
            "review_text": "Kanitgrey\nHanoi, Vietnam6 contributions\n1\nBat Dan, then buy him a beer or ten\nNov 2018 • Friends\nRealistically, the best value restaurant in Hanoi, and probably the best example of classic northern Vietnamese cuisine in Hanoi's Old Quarter. Unfortunately, it is often overlooked by travellers because it: a) looks like a toilet; and b) is generally patronised by large groups of extremely loud and often drunk local men. But please don't let that put you off (try it just outside of peak meal times). As a former resident and now regular business traveller to Hanoi, I have \"dined\" there probably about 200 times over a 12 year period, and am very happy to say that very little has changed during that time. The quality of the food is still outstanding. Try their classics: eel fried in lemongrass and chilli, Sichuan tofu, Bat Dan sausage, dried beef papaya salad, grilled pork ribs, fried betel-leaf wrapped buffalo, squid fried in butter, Vietnamese beefsteak...I could literally keep listing for days. But I won't because I am going their literally right now to consume vast quantities of food and beer again. See ya!\nRead more\nValue\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 17, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
