            "review_text": "Mel F\nBrisbane, Australia23 contributions\n0\nreal Bia Hoi\nJul 2018 • Couples\nauthentic Hanoi Bia Hoi pub. Not fancy but no hawkers like at Bia Hoi corner. Small chairs and tables on the footpath, busy at night because its good and cheap. Mostly locals. You can have the fried sparrow if you want, but the more western-oriented spring rolls and noodles are great, the beer is good and cold, and the location allows great people watching. As always as a tourist in Viet Nam - check price matches menu before agreeing to order.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten July 24, 2018",
